-- title:
--   Cancellation identity for the frozen rounded guarded valuation defect
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be a finite prime-label set and let $B$ be a bridge on the corresponding head tags and a finite band set. Let $R$ be a bank realization at its sample size $n$ and tail endpoint for $c$, with a guarded central-anchor certificate at depth $d$, and let $T$ be a barycentric target. Fix $K_0$, real $\delta_*,\beta_{\rm prot},\beta_{\rm act},\widetilde q$, and a natural prime label $p$. Assume $n\ge1$, $\delta_*\le1$, and every sample value lies in guarded row one at depth parameter $K_0+1$. If $D_p$ is the source frozen rounded smooth-source-to-guarded valuation defect, $s_m$ its top frozen rounded active seed with the post-head-fit balanced alpha, and $V_p^{\rm base}$ its guarded smooth base valuation moment, then
--
--   $$D_p=\sum_m s_m\,v_p(\operatorname{value}(m))-V_p^{\rm base}.$$
--
--   The protected frozen contribution cancels exactly, leaving the active valuation discrepancy.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/ShouqiaoW/erdos/blob/61325b10bbdc29f4fb5e0618b414b9f2189333ad/390/lean/Erdos390/WholePaper/BankPaperCanonicalSmoothSourceGuardedRateClosure.lean#L292-L502

